    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="co_d38">

                <pb facs="co_d38-1" n="1" xml:id="co_d38-1"/>

                <head>CO–38. Telegram from the Acting Secretary of State to the Embassy in
                        Colombia<anchor n="1" xml:id="co_d38-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1960-12-02T18:47:00-05:00">December 2, 1960,
                            6:47 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>361. FOR AMBASSADOR FROM MANN</p>
                <p>Embtel 268<anchor n="2" xml:id="co_d38-f2"/></p>
                <p>Not yet possible furnish any official assurances GOC re U.S. assistance anti-violence program.</p>
                <p>FYI Dept has been actively pushing this matter
                    and necessary Presidential Determination now ready in draft and distributed
                    other <pb facs="0470" n="382" type="typeset" xml:id="pg382"/> agencies. Dept
                    hopes receive all comments and necessary clearances and be in position request
                    White House approval during coming week. Once latter obtained you will be
                    notified soonest.</p>
                <p>END FYI</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold"
                            >Dillon</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">ACTING</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#co_d38-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="co_d38-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Central Files, 721.5-MSP/12–160. Secret. Drafted by
                        Frank J. Devine, Special Assistant
                    to the Assistant Secretary of State for Inter-American Affairs, and signed by
                        Mann.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#co_d38-f2" n="2" xml:id="co_d38-f2-content">
                <p>Telegram 268 form Bogotá, December 1, 1960, reads as follows:<lb/>“There is
                    increasing irritation here at highest government levels at lack U.S. assistance
                    combat violence as requested by President Lleras year and half ago. Important in
                    our interests make immediate decision regarding aid program and implement it
                    quickly.” (721.5–MSP/12–160)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
